    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Document path",
      "items": [
        "Caddy sends document requests to the per-service loopback proxy; other application traffic uses the direct upstream route.",
        "The document proxy injects the script only when devtools are enabled and the response is HTML. Failed document requests can show recovery controls."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Control path",
      "items": [
        "The root-compatible service route exposes /__devhost__/* when devtools are enabled.",
        "The browser fetches uncached instance configuration before mounting React. Control handlers serve assets, streams and stack actions."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Process ownership",
      "items": [
        "The supervisor selects requested services, group members, alwaysStart services and their dependencies, then launches each configured command.",
        "The same supervisor prepares per-service document proxies and registers Caddy routes. The drawing separates request paths from process startup."
      ]
    }
